l scale (e.g., -10: Hostile, 0: Neutral, 10: Friendly) with clear definitions for each level.\\n*   **Ability Status:**\\n    *   Format: Use a table.\\n    *   Columns: Soul Power Level, Soul Rings (Quantity, Age, Source, Skills), Soul Bones (Type, Source, Skills), Special Abilities/Skills, Inventory (Key Items, Resources).\\n\\n**Example Format:**\\n\\n```markdown\\n**Timeline Node: 1.0 (Entering Shrek Academy)**\\n\\n**Relationships:**\\n\\n| Character | Affinity Level | Event | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Bei Bei | -10 | Default | Unfamiliar |\\n| Bei Bei | 10 | 1.1 Follow Bei Bei | Familiar, joined Tang Sect |\\n| Bei Bei | -5 | 1.2 Act Alone |  |\\n| Tang Ya | -10 | Default | Unfamiliar |\\n| Wang Dong | 0 | Default | Not formally acquainted |\\n| ... | ... | ... | ... |\\n\\n**Ability Status:**\\n\\n| Category | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Soul Power Level | 10 |\\n| Soul Rings | 1 (10-year, Tian Meng Ice Silkworm, Mental Detection) |\\n| Soul Bones | None |\\n| Special Abilities | Mental Detection |\\n| Inventory | Key Item: None |\\n\\n**Timeline Node: 1.1 (Choosing to follow Bei Bei)**\\n\\n**Relationships:**\\n ... (Update based on 1.1)\\n ...\\n\\n**Ability Status:**\\n ... (Update based on 1.1)\\n ...\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Note:** Ensure each entry is clearly linked to a specific timeline node and branch. Track changes from the previous node. Describe the mechanisms and rationales behind significant shifts. Provide detailed numerical references for game mechanics where appropriate. These details should provide clear guidance for describing character traits and states during gameplay, informing how choices might influence events and their outcomes. They can offer strategic insights, highlighting potential opportunities and challenges posed by these shifts in relationships or power dynamics. Ensure that you note whether items will interact with other NPCs or organizations and how they're affected by significant plot points. Describe items' special properties,